      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-30-show-hn-tally-check-a-spreadsheet-s-numbers-against-their-so",
      "title": "Show HN: Tally – check a spreadsheet's numbers against their source, in-browser",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://tally.jiegou.ai/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49113381\nPoints: 4\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Does the report you're about to sendactually match your data?\nDrop it here and find out — every figure re-added from the rows underneath, right now, in your browser.\nDrop an .xlsx here, or click to choose\nA summary and the rows behind it — two tabs, or one. Messy is fine. Nothing is uploaded.\norConnect your Google Sheet— Tally re-checks it on a schedule and alerts you when it stops tying out.\n🔒 Your spreadsheet never leaves your browser. Everything here runs on your device.\nHow it fits your workflow\nCheckBefore you hit sendReviewed isn't reconciled. Drop a file — or connect a Google Sheet — and every figure is independently recomputed and reconciled against its own rows, marked ✓ or ✗, with the exact rows as the receipt.\nWatchThen stop thinking about itTally re-pulls a connected sheet daily or weekly, re-verifies every figure unattended, and tells you the moment something stops tying out — or the data changes under a number you already reported. Set up a watch →\nProveSo they stop re-checking youEvery verification becomes a shareable “✓ Verified” link. The person you send it to clicks any figure and sees the rows behind it — proof, not promises.\nSee it catch a real mistake\nA landscaping business's monthly numbers\nGreenEdge tracks jobs on one tab and shows the owner a revenue-by-crew summary on another. This month, one figure doesn't tie out.\n1 The sheet their job log\n2 The report revenue by crew\nOne crew's total is overstated by $3,450 — a job counted twice. Caught before it reached anyone. The mistake is genuinely in the file, not staged.\nTie your sheet out against QuickBooks\nThe harder question: does your report actually agree with your books? Connect QuickBooks and Tally reconciles every figure in your report against your actual invoices — credit memos included — and names the ones that don't tie, with the exact documents as proof. It reads your books read-only and keeps no copy.\nNot ready to connect? Get occasional product updates by email as we add sources.",
