      "body": "Hacker Public Radio is a technology focused podcast that releases shows every weekday Monday to Friday. Our shows are produced by listeners like you and can be on any topic that is of interest to hackers, hobbyists, makers, etc. We are a welcoming community that offers positive feedback and encourages respectful debate.\nLatest Shows\thpr4695 (2026-07-31) :: Try not to buy a phone by operat0r\nPhone setup alternatives, SMS solutions, and challenges with VoIP numbers.        hpr4694 (2026-07-30) :: HPR Beer Garden 16 - Belgian Blonde by Kevie\nKevie and Dave talk about Belgian Blonde Ales        hpr4693 (2026-07-29) :: Amateur Radio Field Days by Archer72\nArcher72 talks briefly about the worldwide Amateur Radio Field Days        hpr4692 (2026-07-28) :: Noise Music Tutorial 2: Using Audacity to Make Noise by TheDUDE\nA tutorial and explainging different ways to make Noise music using audacity        hpr4691 (2026-07-27) :: Viva la Coda by Lee\nor C++ and all its friends        hpr4690 (2026-07-24) :: Playing Civilization V, Part 14 by Ahuka\nWe conclude a sample game of Civilization V        hpr4689 (2026-07-23) :: Cheap Yellow Display Project Part 8: Writing the code  by Trey\nHow we wrote the code to make this whole thing work        hpr4688 (2026-07-22) :: Downloading Podcasts with a Shell Script by Whiskeyjack\nThe basic principles of downloading podcasts using your own shell scripts.        hpr4687 (2026-07-21) :: UNIX Curio #11 - Merging Files by Vance\nBringing your data together        hpr4686 (2026-07-20) :: Debugging Security Cameras: Firmware Updates, Python Scripts and Windows Workarounds by operat0r\nDebug a Uniview camera using Python scripts, firmware updates and Windows hacks.",
