      "title": "Show HN: Echologue – the private AI voice journal I built for myself",
      "summary": "I have tried journaling many times but nothing stuck. So I decided to make my own app for myself with these features:\n* Voice first\n* Private first\n* AI chat\n* Automatic tagging, meaning extraction, and semantic retrieval using embeddings stored locally\n* Export to LLM\nthe AI angle is especially interesting for me. It allows me to ask questions like:\n* \"remind me highlights and crazy nights in the",
      "body": "Now Available · Local-First · iPhone + Android\nA PRIVATE VOICE JOURNAL YOU CAN ASK LATER.\nEchologue turns quick voice notes and private journal entries into a memory you can actually come back to. Capture moments, moods, and fleeting realizations — then ask grounded questions across your own history. Not a generic chatbot. Your own memory, made askable.\nVOICE NOTE IN. MEMORY OUT.\nRecord the messy version: what happened, who was there, how it felt, and the small thought you do not want to lose. Echologue turns it into structured memory you can ask about later.\n\"Last day in Barcelona. Walked through the Gothic Quarter with Leo, had paella near Barceloneta, and felt lighter than I have in weeks.\"\nFactsBarcelona · Leo · Gothic Quarter · Barceloneta · paella\nFeelingsLighter · relaxed · more open than the weeks before\nASK\"What were the highlights of my Barcelona trip?\"\nRECALLA grounded answer from your own entries — not generic chatbot memory.\nMost journals are great for capture and terrible for retrieval. Echologue turns raw voice notes and journal entries into something you can come back to with real questions — whenever you want grounded recall from your own life.\nEntries become retrievable memory instead of dead text. Ask about a person, trip, mood, or time period and get an answer grounded in what you actually recorded.\nWhen you ask \"how did I feel about that trip?\" the answer is only useful if what happened and how you felt are tracked separately. That separation is what makes recall trustworthy instead of vague.\nYour journal lives on your device. AI processing is ephemeral, remembered chat is explicit, and export or wipe controls stay in your hands.\nYou already dictate thoughts, memories, afterthoughts, or messy personal notes and want them to become useful later.\nYou care less about polished prose and more about remembering what happened, how it felt, and what keeps recurring.\nYou want AI recall, but you do not want your permanent personal archive to become someone else’s cloud database.\nPeople who want real recall\nYou want your notes to answer questions later, not sit in a folder where useful details quietly disappear.\nLow-friction journaling in, grounded recall out — for lived moments and thoughts you would otherwise lose.\n01 / CaptureCapture Raw Life\nSpeak a quick voice memo or write a short entry. Capture what happened, how you felt, or a thought you do not want to lose — not polished prose.\n02 / StructureTurn It Into Memory\nEchologue separates facts from feelings, extracts people and themes, and indexes entries so your history becomes searchable by meaning instead of folders or endless threads.\n03 / AskGet Grounded Recall\nAsk what changed, what keeps recurring, or how you usually feel around someone. Answers are pulled from your own entries instead of generic memoryless chat.\nASK BETTER QUESTIONS THAN SEARCH CAN HANDLE.\nEchologue is strongest when you want grounded recall, not just storage. These are the kinds of questions the product is built around.\n01 / TripsGive me the highlights of my trip in Barcelona.\nPull together what happened, who was there, and how it felt across multiple entries — without scrolling through a month of journal.\n02 / PeopleHow do I usually feel around this person?\nTrace repeated emotional patterns around specific people without rereading dozens of entries.\n03 / InsightsWhat small insights keep coming back?\nSurface repeated realizations, recurring self-advice, or small mental notes that would otherwise evaporate after the day ends.\n\"Last day in Barcelona. Walked through the Gothic Quarter with Leo in the morning, then spent the afternoon at Barceloneta. The paella was incredible. Felt lighter than I have in weeks.\"\n\"Give me the highlights of my trip in Barcelona.\"\nYour Barcelona trip was mostly with Leo over 4 days. Highlights: the Gothic Quarter walk, the long afternoon at Barceloneta, paella on the last day. You mentioned feeling lighter and more relaxed than the weeks before the trip.\nBUILT FOR RECALL, NOT JUST CAPTURE.\nUse voice when typing is too much friction. Everyday moments, conversations, afterthoughts, and small realizations become part of a journal you can return to later.\nAsk about people, places, moods, or time periods in natural language and retrieve the entries that actually matter, even when you do not remember the exact words.\nEach entry is organized into facts, feelings, entities, and themes so your history stays legible whether you are recalling a trip, a person, or a fleeting realization.\nEchologue can reason over what has been happening lately without losing your broader personal history, making recall feel both current and grounded.\nYour journal stays on your device. AI processing is ephemeral, and export, backup, and wipe controls keep ownership with you.\nExport your journal as JSON or CSV, keep your own backup, wipe the app anytime, or bring your archive to another AI tool if you choose.\nDictate in many languages and turn voice notes into structured entries. Transcription quality can vary by language, accent, and audio clarity.\nRemembered chat is visible and intentional. Useful clarifications can become memory, while off-the-record conversations stay out of the profile.\nSTART FREE. UPGRADE WHEN IT BECOMES A HABIT.\nEchologue is built to be useful from the first few voice notes. Start with the free tier, then upgrade when private recall becomes part of your daily rhythm.\nA real starting point for trying private voice journaling and grounded recall without committing first.\n20 voice notes per month.\n15 voice minutes per month.\n10 AI replies per month.\nLocal-first journal storage and export.\nFor people who use Echologue regularly and want more voice capture, more recall, and more control over how the app responds.\n500 voice minutes per month.\n400 AI replies per month.\nCustom personas for different kinds of reflection.\nEverything stays portable, exportable, and wipeable.\nEchologue is especially useful for people who already journal, use voice memos, keep personal notes, or want a private AI memory layer for their own life.\nGET ECHOLOGUE ON YOUR PHONE.\nInstall Echologue from the app stores, start with a few short voice notes, then ask what your own history remembers.\niPhone on the App Store.\nNo account required for your local journal archive.\nGet the private memory app.\nInstall Echologue from the app stores and start with a few short entries. Your permanent journal archive stays on your device.\nFree to start. Premium unlocks higher monthly usage and advanced memory controls.\nYOUR DATA STAYS. AI VISITS.\nYour journal, memories, and profile live on your device — that is where the permanent record exists. When AI helps structure an entry or answer a question, processing is ephemeral. The product is designed so your archive remains yours, portable, and not platform data.\nStored on your device. Entries, semantic memory, remembered chats, and your evolving profile never leave your phone as stored data.\nAI content is processed using zero-data-retention controls and is not used to train AI models. Limited technical request metadata may still be processed or retained.\nRemembering is explicit. You choose whether a chat becomes part of memory or stays off the record.\nExport or wipe anytime. Keep a local JSON/CSV backup, move your memories elsewhere, or bring them to another AI tool if you choose. No account required — no server archive to delete.\n\"A journal should help youremember, not just record.\"\nMost journals are write-only. Most chat apps forget everything or flatten it into one endless thread. Echologue is built for the middle: private capture, structured recall, and answers grounded in your own history.",
