      "id": "bbc-2026-07-26-after-chaotic-return-where-does-joshua-win-leave-fury-fight",
      "title": "After chaotic return, where does Joshua win leave Fury fight?",
      "summary": "Where does Anthony Joshua's chaotic comeback win over Kristian Prenga leave the super-fight with Tyson Fury?",
      "body": "In the aftermath of such a chaotic night, it is easy to focus only on the flaws and forget the bigger picture. Joshua was returning from one of the darkest periods of his life and carrying an immense emotional burden into the ring.After his hand was raised, he struggled to get through his interview. His voice cracked as he spoke about his two friends and the impact their loss has had on him.\"Boxing once saved him and he needed boxing to get through this. That camp allowed him to focus his mind while he was in so much grief and pain,\" promoter Eddie Hearn said.\"You don't know what he was going through in that camp because he doesn't talk about it.\"Whatever happens next, his place in British boxing history is already secure. He is an Olympic gold medallist, a two-time heavyweight champion and one of the biggest sporting stars this country has produced.He has taken boxing to places few British fighters ever have. He has filled stadiums, headlined global events and become a household name far beyond the sport.But in the build-up to his comeback, Joshua and his stablemate Oleksandr Usyk spoke about the ambition of becoming undisputed heavyweight champion.After Saturday night in Saudi, the reality is that even reclaiming a world title would be a tough ask.Joshua has always spoken about legacy, and there would be something fitting about walking away after overcoming one of the toughest periods of his life and producing a dramatic comeback victory.The danger with ageing fighters is chasing one more night. Boxing history is filled with champions who stayed that one fight too long.But then again Fury-Joshua is not one more fight. It is the fight. The one that has loomed over their careers for the best part of a decade.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-26T07:33:35.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/6cd0/live/5b4574b0-8891-11f1-9694-4f3a1914e2ba.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/boxing/articles/cgr7gyv8zq0o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-07-26-it-was-like-a-movie-i-looked-up-and-an-exploded-barn-rained-",
      "title": "'It was like a movie - I looked up and an exploded barn rained on me'",
      "summary": "Photographer Scott Johnson's studio is close to where a fire triggered a massive explosion.",
      "body": "The photographer was driving to his studio for a meeting when he realised the fire on the horizon was at the farm where it was based.\"It was about 150 metres (492ft) from my front door, and I quickly cancelled the meeting and thought, 'I'm not happy with where the wind is going on this',\" he said.Johnson began removing some of his more expensive kit from the studio and was putting it in the van when the explosion took place. A unit housing fertiliser had exploded.He said: \"It blew me into the door and I just ran to the van, dropped the bit I went back in for - maybe it saved my life, I don't know.\"As it happened: Twenty firefighters taken to hospital after major Essex explosionThe photographer was shocked to see his studio roof had completely caved in.Having driven to a safe distance, \"I pulled over, and I was just in shock and started to shake\", he said, although he was reassured after an ambulance crew checked him over.Johnson managed to cover his wedding booking on Saturday, praising his \"amazing assistant\" James Musselwhite for driving from Portsmouth to help him out.\"I'm in a little bit of shock still, to be honest,\" he said. \"I'm completely unscathed apart from a bit of a dodgy ear from the pressure - but how I've got away with it unscathed I have no idea.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-26T06:57:06.000Z",
