      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-25-warner-bros-lawsuit-accuses-amazon-of-illegally-poaching-exe",
      "title": "Warner Bros. lawsuit accuses Amazon of illegally poaching executives",
      "summary": "The lawsuit will likely renew debates about whether term employment agreements are enforceable under California. law",
      "body": "1:55 PM PDT · July 25, 2026\nImage Credits:Victor J. Blue/Bloomberg / Getty Images\nWarner Bros. Discovery filed a lawsuit this week accusing Amazon of interference with contractual relations, breach of contract, and unfair competition.\nAs reported by Deadline, the lawsuit alleges Amazon has been “hurriedly seeking to pirate away a number of contracted employees,” including Pia Barlow, an HBO Max marketing executive who recently joined Amazon MGM Studios. Warner Bros. (whose pending acquisition by Paramount has been paused for at least a few months) said Barlow’s employment contract was “not set to expire until October 31, 2027.”\n“In blatant disregard of established California law, Amazon has gone rogue by attempting to induce Plaintiffs’ employees with term employment agreements to breach those agreements with impunity, backed up with the ready assurance that Amazon will defend and indemnify them should they be held to account for their blatantly unlawful acts,” Warner Bros. said.\nThe company also accused Amazon of seeking to “tortiously induce another WBD employee to breach their term employment agreement, which was not set to expire until December 2027,” although that executive (believed to be HBO programming executive Francesca Orsi) ultimately stayed at Warner Bros.\nDeadline noted that this lawsuit is likely to renew debates about whether term employment agreements are actually enforceable under California law.\nAmazon MGM Studios declined to comment.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news\nLatest in Government & Policy",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Anthony Ha",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-25T20:55:11.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/warner-bros.jpg?resize=1200,800",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/25/warner-bros-lawsuit-accuses-amazon-of-illegally-poaching-executives/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
